---
description: When tests may change production code
globs: services/**,workers/**,shared/**,infra/**,migrations/**,frontend/**
alwaysApply: false
---
Allowed:
1. Small behaviour-neutral testability seams (env-driven connections, timing knobs, test ids, healthchecks).
2. Fixes for a defect already recorded as BUG-n, in the same change that flips its xfail(strict), with a KNOWN_ISSUES.md update.
3. Mechanical hygiene in files the task already touches: lifespan instead of on_event, Annotated aliases, model_config, status.HTTP_*, pathlib.
Not allowed now: layered restructuring, async rewrite of scheduler-worker, uv/pyproject per service, src/ move, nginx limit changes (BUG-1), outbox (BUG-3), idempotency key change (BUG-7).
Every prod edit is listed in KNOWN_ISSUES.md ("Testability changes" or the bug's status).